-8. Permissions, privacy and security
-Permission / capability	Policy
-BLUETOOTH (legacy)	Declare only where needed for older Android versions; runtime model differs by OS.
-BLUETOOTH_ADMIN (legacy)	Only for legacy scanning/connection behaviour where required.
-BLUETOOTH_CONNECT	Request on Android 12+ when connecting to paired Bluetooth devices.
-BLUETOOTH_SCAN	Only if scanning for adapters; explain purpose. Avoid location inference if not needed.
-ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION	Only if GPS trip recording or map feature requires precise location; ask separately and allow core OBD without it.
-FOREGROUND_SERVICE	Only for user-visible active session; comply with target SDK service type rules.
-INTERNET	Only for map provider, optional updates or user-requested online features; core OBD remains offline.
-
-•	No account required for core app.
-•	Do not upload VIN, GPS routes, DTCs or vehicle logs by default.
-•	Offer export/delete all local data.
-•	Do not put VIN, GPS or diagnostic data in analytics/crash logs.
-•	API keys must be restricted and kept out of public source where possible; explain local build configuration.
-•	Never transmit arbitrary CAN frames from a UI text field in normal release builds.
-•	Do not run actuator tests or clear safety-module faults in the initial release.
-9. Safety and responsible diagnostics
-Safety boundary
-This is a monitoring and diagnostic aid, not a safety-certified instrument cluster. Do not present OBD speed as the vehicle's legally authoritative speedometer. Do not encourage phone interaction while driving. All detailed diagnostics, code clearing, configuration, performance tests and exports should be parked-only or require a deliberate safety gate.
-
-•	Use GPS speed only as a secondary display and label its source; do not replace factory speedometer.
-•	Sensor thresholds must be configurable and sourced; account for operating conditions.
-•	Never state that a component is safe or defective based on one PID.
-•	Before clearing DTCs, explain data/readiness loss and ask for confirmation.
-•	Do not expose Mode 08 control, raw CAN write or proprietary security access in the initial release.
-•	Do not provide ECU flashing, immobilizer, key programming, airbag activation/deactivation or emissions defeat functions.
- 
