-11. Test plan and acceptance criteria
-11.1 Unit tests
-•	ELM response normalisation: echoed command, prompt, CR/LF, NO DATA, STOPPED, ERROR, malformed bytes.
-•	PID decoders: positive test vectors, short payload, extra bytes, invalid values and units.
-•	DTC parsing: stored/pending/permanent, multiple codes, zero codes, malformed response.
-•	ISO-TP multi-frame assembly and flow control if implemented.
-•	Supported-PID bitmap parsing and recursive discovery.
-•	Fuel and trip calculations with zero distance, missing MAF, invalid GPS and stale samples.
-•	Data freshness transitions and reconnect state machine.
-•	Room migrations and export serialization.
-11.2 Integration and device tests
-Test	Pass condition
-No adapter	App opens; all pages work in Demo Mode; clear disconnected state.
-Unsupported adapter	Useful explanation; no crash or endless spinner.
-ELM327 Bluetooth Classic	Pair/connect; initialise; read supported PIDs; disconnect cleanly.
-Adapter clone / slow response	Timeout/retry logic; low-bandwidth mode; no command interleaving.
-Vehicle ignition off	Graceful timeout; no false sensor values.
-Engine running	Live values update; stale state when responses stop.
-S24 Ultra portrait	No clipping/overlap; accessible text; all actions usable.
-S24 Ultra landscape	Adaptive cockpit layout; panels resize and page navigation works.
-Large landscape display	Map/telemetry split; no fixed pixel assumptions.
-Waze installed / absent	Deep link opens Waze or gives fallback instructions.
-No network / no Maps key	OBD and local features still work; map panel explains offline/unconfigured state.
-Process recreation	Saved preferences and records remain; connection recovers safely.
-
-11.3 Performance targets
-•	No UI thread blocking from Bluetooth, database, chart rendering or parsing.
-•	Dashboard remains responsive while telemetry is active.
-•	Bounded log storage with configurable retention; avoid unbounded high-frequency raw data.
-•	Battery use is measured in active and background modes.
-•	Reconnect backoff prevents rapid repeated connection loops.
-•	Charts downsample long histories for rendering without deleting raw stored data.
-12. Data schema — minimum viable
-Entity	Important fields
-Vehicle	id, make, model, year, market, engine, transmission, VIN (optional), createdAt
-Adapter	id, displayName, address/id, transportType, adapterVersion, lastSeen, notes
-EcuIdentity	vehicleId, ecuHeader, protocol, calibrationId, cvn, source, observedAt
-PidCapability	vehicleId, ecuHeader, service, pid, supported, verification, discoveredAt
-SensorSample	sessionId, pidKey, value, unit, timestamp, source, quality
-DtcRecord	vehicleId, code, status, ecuHeader, firstSeen, lastSeen, freezeFrameRef
-Trip	id, vehicleId, start, end, distance, duration, idleDuration, fuelEstimate, routeOptIn
-MaintenanceEntry	id, vehicleId, item, date, odometer, cost, currency, notes
-DashboardPage	id, name, order, visible, widgetLayoutJson, defaultPage
-AppSettings	theme, units, currency, pollingProfile, safetyOptions, mapProvider
-
-Use migrations and stable IDs. Avoid storing every high-rate sample forever; provide session summaries and user-configurable retention. Encrypt particularly sensitive optional data where appropriate; VIN and route history should be treated as personal data.
